1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,799
Verifying complex Ethereum protocol

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,960
requirements against the actual

3
00:00:04,799 --> 00:00:08,960
implementation code is a demanding

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,960
engineering task. If you want to

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:13,440
automate that process using an AI

6
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:15,759
workflow, you have to ensure the system

7
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:17,920
actually traces the high-level rules

8
00:00:15,759 --> 00:00:20,000
directly to the underlying repository

9
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:23,359
logic. That was the goal of a

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,359
verification project called EIP verify.

11
00:00:23,359 --> 00:00:27,119
The researchers wanted to see if an AI

12
00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:29,279
could map the strict demands of the

13
00:00:27,119 --> 00:00:32,000
protocol to the specific lines of code

14
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:34,079
that execute them. During testing, the

15
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,800
workflow produced a strange operational

16
00:00:34,079 --> 00:00:38,640
paradox. A single run generated two

17
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,960
distinct artifacts that were supposed to

18
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:43,600
agree with each other. The first was a

19
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:46,160
highly polished fluent summary report.

20
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:48,480
The second was the raw rowle spreadsheet

21
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:50,079
containing the actual evidence. The

22
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,239
problem was that they told two

23
00:00:50,079 --> 00:00:54,000
completely different stories. The

24
00:00:52,239 --> 00:00:55,760
polished summary confidently claimed

25
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,920
that every single obligation was

26
00:00:55,760 --> 00:01:00,480
properly mapped, but checking the raw

27
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:02,640
spreadsheet exposed critical errors. The

28
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:05,920
raw data revealed mappings that pointed

29
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:07,760
to irrelevant test fixtures and RPC glue

30
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:10,080
completely missing the protocol logic

31
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:12,159
the system was supposed to verify. The

32
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:14,720
system was confident, but the evidence

33
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:17,920
was wrong. This creates a dangerous

34
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:20,240
asymmetry based entirely on legibility.

35
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:22,240
Without an explicit rule to stop it, the

36
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:24,720
incorrect polished summary naturally

37
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:27,119
moves downstream. It gets pasted into a

38
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:30,000
readme, used in a deployment argument,

39
00:01:27,119 --> 00:01:32,000
or sent to a fun. The accurate, messier

40
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,400
spreadsheet stays technically available,

41
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,400
but is operationally ignored. This

42
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:38,640
dynamic illustrates a problem we call

43
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,240
confidence debt. A system incurs

44
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:42,720
confidence debt when its output is

45
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:45,040
trusted downstream before the verifiable

46
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:46,880
evidence actually warrants that trust.

47
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:49,040
The trust propagates faster than the

48
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:51,200
proof. To understand how this debt

49
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:53,360
compounds, we have to look at the three

50
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,079
layers of the AI deployment pipeline,

51
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:58,719
artifacts, evaluations, and humans.

52
00:01:56,079 --> 00:02:01,119
Relying on fluent AI outputs without

53
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:03,439
verifying their epistemic texture breaks

54
00:02:01,119 --> 00:02:05,600
the engineering pipeline. By the time a

55
00:02:03,439 --> 00:02:07,759
human makes a decision, the workflow has

56
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,440
preserved the machine's conclusion while

57
00:02:07,759 --> 00:02:11,840
stripping away the user's right to

58
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:14,080
dispute it. The cascade begins at the

59
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:16,400
artifact layer, where the raw outputs

60
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:18,879
are first generated. Think of a language

61
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:21,120
model as an industrial compressor. To

62
00:02:18,879 --> 00:02:24,080
generate a readable summary, the system

63
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:26,160
crushes down the data. This compression

64
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:28,239
mechanism inherently strips away the

65
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:30,720
caveats, the source paths, and the

66
00:02:28,239 --> 00:02:33,200
contradictions. Those jagged edges are

67
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:35,360
removed to maintain narrative fluency.

68
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:37,200
In standard engineering workflows, these

69
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:39,440
compressed summaries automatically

70
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:41,599
outrank the raw sources. A clean

71
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:43,680
paragraph is simply easier to read and

72
00:02:41,599 --> 00:02:45,920
share than a complicated spreadsheet. So

73
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:48,080
it gets prioritized. This initial

74
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:49,920
transfer of borrowed trust means the

75
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:51,760
underlying data becomes completely

76
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:54,560
untethered from the deployment arguments

77
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:57,680
made downstream. The evidence gets left

78
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:59,920
behind. Fixing this requires inserting

79
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,440
our first structural checkpoint into the

80
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:06,080
workflow. Gate one. Gate one enforces

81
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:08,159
the rule of claim auditability. It

82
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:10,159
dictates that no claim can be promoted

83
00:03:08,159 --> 00:03:12,800
to the next stage based solely on how

84
00:03:10,159 --> 00:03:14,959
well it reads. The output cannot pass

85
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:18,080
until the summary expands back into an

86
00:03:14,959 --> 00:03:20,000
inspectable state. In engineering terms,

87
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:21,920
a claim must permanently attach an

88
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,480
evidence ledger, a contradiction

89
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:27,200
register, and an expiry condition before

90
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:29,120
moving forward. The polished summary is

91
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:31,840
no longer allowed to outrank the raw

92
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:34,319
data. Claim auditability stops the

93
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:35,680
earliest stage of confidence debt. It

94
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:37,840
forces the evidence to travel

95
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:39,440
concurrently with the narrative output,

96
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:42,080
ensuring the proof survives the

97
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:44,239
compression process. Once the artifacts

98
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:46,720
are generated, the workflow moves to the

99
00:03:44,239 --> 00:03:49,120
second stage, testing at the evaluation

100
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:52,080
layer. Here we encounter the operational

101
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:54,239
hazard of benchmarks. Converting complex

102
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:56,480
performance data into a single score

103
00:03:54,239 --> 00:03:58,720
metric strips away of the operational

104
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:01,120
caveats, turning them into pure

105
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:03,760
numerical confidence debt. This bar

106
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:06,159
chart shows GPT40's performance on the

107
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:08,879
TOW bench benchmark for retail domain

108
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:11,920
tasks. The pass at one metric is marked

109
00:04:08,879 --> 00:04:13,840
here at 61%. A team looking at that

110
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:16,720
single number might conclude the model

111
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:19,519
is ready, but pass at one only measures

112
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:21,759
execution of an isolated task once under

113
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:24,800
clean conditions. Watch what happens

114
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:27,680
when we adjust the Xaxis to evaluate

115
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:30,960
pass at 8, meaning repeated sustained

116
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:32,560
runs. The performance bar crashes below

117
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:34,560
25%.

118
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:37,040
The model didn't lose its base

119
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:40,560
capability. It failed because of

120
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:43,280
trajectory drift. In long horizon tasks,

121
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:45,360
capable agents slowly diverge from the

122
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:47,680
paths that successful runs tend to

123
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:51,120
follow, turning coherent partial

124
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:53,520
progress into unreoverable errors. Clean

125
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:55,759
benchmark scores hide the reality of

126
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:57,759
production environments. They don't

127
00:04:55,759 --> 00:05:00,560
account for network timeouts, rate

128
00:04:57,759 --> 00:05:03,360
limits, schema drift, or sudden partial

129
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:06,720
progress meltdowns. This requires our

130
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:08,960
second structural checkpoint, gate 2. To

131
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:10,400
evaluate correctly, we replace the

132
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:12,639
single bar chart with a

133
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:15,440
three-dimensional surface plot. This

134
00:05:12,639 --> 00:05:17,520
graph's repeated consistency, robustness

135
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:20,479
against task variations, and fault

136
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:22,960
tolerance. This enforces reliability

137
00:05:20,479 --> 00:05:24,800
release. It mandates that a single

138
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:27,520
benchmark score cannot license

139
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:29,520
deployment readiness alone. Systems must

140
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:32,479
be strictly scoped to a measured

141
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:34,479
operational envelope. You predefine your

142
00:05:32,479 --> 00:05:36,880
systems tolerances for specific

143
00:05:34,479 --> 00:05:39,759
perturbations and failures and release

144
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:42,160
it only within those proven boundaries.

145
00:05:39,759 --> 00:05:44,639
Forcing a reliability release ensures

146
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:46,800
that the evaluation layer cannot finance

147
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:49,919
false deployment arguments based on

148
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:52,080
irrelevant oneshot metrics. That brings

149
00:05:49,919 --> 00:05:54,720
us to the final stage of the pipeline,

150
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:56,800
the human layer. The industry typically

151
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:59,039
relies on a human in the loop to catch

152
00:05:56,800 --> 00:06:00,880
the errors that slip through. This

153
00:05:59,039 --> 00:06:03,840
approach introduces a serious

154
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:06,080
operational paradox. Placing a tired

155
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:09,039
human reviewer in front of highly fluent

156
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:12,000
AI output actively degrades operational

157
00:06:09,039 --> 00:06:14,639
safety. Look at how an AI presents its

158
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:17,280
answer. The sleek text output sits

159
00:06:14,639 --> 00:06:19,600
directly on top of the raw data, hiding

160
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:22,240
the massive tangled web of logic from

161
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:24,800
the reviewer. This creates what is known

162
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:27,280
as the competence shadow. The AI

163
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:29,680
artificially prunes the problem space,

164
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:31,680
removing specific hazards, alternative

165
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:34,240
solutions, and contradictions from the

166
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:36,160
visible discussion. A cognitive hazard

167
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:38,080
forms because the human reviewer can

168
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:40,319
only evaluate the information left on

169
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:41,919
the screen. They cannot inspect or

170
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:44,560
correct the branches of evidence that

171
00:06:41,919 --> 00:06:46,319
the AI secretly omitted. Studies show

172
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:48,720
this degrades engineering skill over

173
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:50,720
time. When developers treat AI as a

174
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:53,120
contractor and themselves merely as

175
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:54,400
reviewers, they lose persistence and the

176
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:56,720
capacity to solve problems

177
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:58,960
independently. Adding a warning label

178
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:01,120
next to the output or asking the user to

179
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:03,440
click an approve button does absolutely

180
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:05,199
nothing to stop this cognitive erosion.

181
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:08,400
We have to install the final checkpoint

182
00:07:05,199 --> 00:07:10,800
in the pipeline, gate 3. We apply gate 3

183
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:12,880
using a hypothesisdriven interface. It

184
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:14,880
extracts individual claims, highlights

185
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:16,800
unsupported statements in red and

186
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:19,120
actively surfaces alternative counter

187
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:21,360
evidence nodes. This is co- audit

188
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:23,120
software. Its entire function is to

189
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:25,120
shift the AI's output from something

190
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:27,440
passively consumed into something that

191
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:30,080
the human must actively work against.

192
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:32,080
The UI forces assumption checking. It

193
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:34,400
strictly demands that the reviewer

194
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:36,319
resolve the presented counter evidence

195
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:38,880
before an acceptance click is

196
00:07:36,319 --> 00:07:41,280
mathematically allowed. Co- audit

197
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:43,919
transforms human oversight into an

198
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:46,400
active epistemic defense, halting the

199
00:07:43,919 --> 00:07:49,199
final transfer of confidence debt right

200
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:51,199
before it translates into action. When

201
00:07:49,199 --> 00:07:53,759
we zoom out and look at the entire

202
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:55,919
repaired pipeline, we see exactly how

203
00:07:53,759 --> 00:07:59,039
the initial problem compounds if left

204
00:07:55,919 --> 00:08:00,960
unchecked. In an unmitigated cascade,

205
00:07:59,039 --> 00:08:04,080
artifact confidence outruns the

206
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:06,800
evidence. Then, evaluation scores outrun

207
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:08,879
actual reliability. Finally, human

208
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:11,599
acceptance outruns our capacity to

209
00:08:08,879 --> 00:08:13,599
notice and correct errors. The standard

210
00:08:11,599 --> 00:08:16,240
industry goal of teaching users

211
00:08:13,599 --> 00:08:18,720
appropriate reliance fails because it

212
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:20,879
happens too late. User calibration

213
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:23,759
cannot fix evidence that was already

214
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:25,440
overcompressed three steps upstream.

215
00:08:23,759 --> 00:08:28,080
Look at the structural layout of the

216
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:29,840
reinforced pipeline. The flow of data is

217
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:32,479
governed by these three distinct

218
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:34,959
checkpoints. Claim auditability before

219
00:08:32,479 --> 00:08:37,440
trust, reliability release before

220
00:08:34,959 --> 00:08:40,080
deployment, and co-odit before human

221
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:42,159
acceptance. Building governable AI

222
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:44,880
systems does not require waiting years

223
00:08:42,159 --> 00:08:46,800
for flawless hallucinationfree models.

224
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:49,519
It requires engineering the workflow

225
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:51,200
around the model's limitations. Today,

226
00:08:49,519 --> 00:08:53,200
safety is achieved by designing

227
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:55,360
workflows that explicitly preserve the

228
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:58,680
human right of dispute at every single

229
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:58,680
layer of delegation.

